      "side": 1,
      "message": "Bentley-Ottmann is not a viable algorithm for computing crossings when using rounding. For Bently-Ottmann to work you need exact arithmetic. There are a couple of straight forward examples to demonstrate this fact which I can show you. I\u0027m characterizing the performance of the Myers algorithm right now, and it seems to be fast.\n\nWe should set up a meeting to discuss this.",
